  "term": "computational model",
  "definition": "A computational model is a computer-based representation of a real system that uses mathematical equations and simulated conditions to predict how that system behaves. In the source, it is used to represent the human eye and estimate drug movement, concentration, and half-life under different physiological scenarios.",
