      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s general statement that a computational model is “a computer-based representation of a real system” using “mathematical equations and simulated conditions to predict how that system behaves” is not explicitly supported by the provided packet text (the packet describes one specific pharmacokinetic modeling approach rather than stating this general definition).",
        "The definition claims the model is used to “estimate drug movement,” but the packet text specifically describes predicting ocular pharmacokinetics, including drug concentration near the macula and intravitreal half-lives; it does not explicitly describe “drug movement.”",
        "The definition is framed as applicable in the “learning” field, but the packet context is an ocular pharmacokinetics/computational modeling study (ranibizumab eye modeling), not learning."
